<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdagases I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdagases I was an Indo-Parthian king of the 1st century CE, a nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gondophares">Gondophares</a> according to his coins. He ruled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> and Gandhara after his uncle, as the kingdom broke up among several successors. He is known mainly from coins with Greek and Kharoshthi legends.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdagases-i.jpg" alt="Abdagases I" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abdagases_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
